.TH SDL_HINT_WAVE_RIFF_CHUNK_SIZE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WAVE_RIFF_CHUNK_SIZE \- A variable controlling how the size of the RIFF chunk affects the loading of a WAVE file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WAVE_RIFF_CHUNK_SIZE \(dqSDL_WAVE_RIFF_CHUNK_SIZE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The size of the RIFF chunk (which includes all the sub-chunks of the WAVE file) is not always reliable\[char46] In case the size is wrong, it\(aqs possible to just ignore it and step through the chunks until a fixed limit is reached\[char46]
.PP
Note that files that have trailing data unrelated to the WAVE file or corrupt files may slow down the loading process without a reliable boundary\[char46] By default, SDL stops after 10000 chunks to prevent wasting time\[char46] Use
.BR SDL_HINT_WAVE_CHUNK_LIMIT
to adjust this value\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqforce\(dq - Always use the RIFF chunk size as a boundary for the chunk search\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqignorezero\(dq - Like \(dqforce\(dq, but a zero size searches up to 4 GiB\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqignore\(dq - Ignore the RIFF chunk size and always search up to 4 GiB\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqmaximum\(dq - Search for chunks until the end of file\[char46] (not recommended)
.PP
This hint should be set before calling
.BR SDL_LoadWAV ()
or
.BR SDL_LoadWAV_IO ()

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

